.TH geectl-build-fileinfo 1  "geectl-build-fileinfo 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-fileinfo \- Read the metadata of a built file: RPM header fields plus dependency lists
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build fileinfo\fR [\fB\-\-ext\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> <\fIFILENAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the metadata of a built file: RPM header fields plus dependency lists
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ext\fR
The `fileinfo_ext` view: each dependency names the packages providing or requiring it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package the file belongs to
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the file was built in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the file was built for
.TP
<\fIFILENAME\fR>
The file to read the metadata for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
